# =============================================================================
# HireSnap backend - build context filter for a STANDALONE build.
#
# WHERE THIS FILE IS ACTUALLY READ: nowhere, in the stack as shipped.
# The compose files build the backend with "context: .." and
# "dockerfile: ./backend/docker/Dockerfile" (docker/docker-compose.yaml:224-227,
# mirroring R:\GPTHub\docker\docker-compose.yaml:32-37), so the context root is
# the SUPERPROJECT and Docker reads the root .dockerignore, not this file.
#
# WHY "docker build backend/" IS NOT A SUPPORTED PATH (measured, not assumed):
# every COPY source in backend/docker/Dockerfile is written with the backend/
# prefix (requirements.txt, requirements-platform.txt, requirements.lock.txt,
# service/, database/), because the build context IS the superproject root.
# Building with the backend directory as the context fails immediately with
# "failed to compute cache key: ... /backend/requirements.txt not found"
# (backend/docker/Dockerfile:145 and the three sibling COPY lines). This file
# therefore filters the STANDALONE case only: backend/ is also a valid checkout
# on its own remote and branch, and a future Dockerfile that does not prefix its
# sources would read these rules. Do not quote it as protection for the stack
#
# WHY an ignore list at all: BuildKit ships every file it is not told to skip to
# the daemon BEFORE it reads the Dockerfile. backend/ carries HireSnap.sql, a
# venv, pytest caches and - on the ML path - model weights; a 20 GB vendor/ or
# weights/ directory turns a 30-second build into a ten-minute one, and on a
# remote daemon into a failed upload (R:\GPTHub\.dockerignore:1-14 makes the
# same argument for the GPTHub root).
#
# The Dockerfile itself is NOT ignored here: BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore
# when it exists, and "backend/docker/Dockerfile.dockerignore" is the escape
# hatch if a context ever needs different rules than this file.
# =============================================================================

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The backend reads configuration from backend/.env (backend/env.py loads the
# dotenv file next to itself). Real values must never be baked into an image
# layer: layers are readable by anyone who can pull, and "docker history" shows
# the filesystem diff. Only the template is allowed through.
# Mirror of R:\GPTHub\.dockerignore:3-5.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- VCS --------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- JWT material ---------------------------------------------------------
# service/certs is the packaged fallback location for the RS256 key pair that
# signs every issued token (service/domain/models.py:_key_path). In the stack the
# pair is a read-only bind mount at /app/secrets/certs
# (docker/docker-compose.yaml) so that tokens stay valid across a rebuild; baking
# it in would ship one deployment's private key inside a distributable artifact.
service/certs
certs
*.pem
*.key

# --- Python environment and caches ----------------------------------------
venv
.venv
env/
ENV/
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# --- runtime state the container mounts instead ---------------------------
# Uploaded videos / embeddings (DATA_PATH), logs and model weights are HOST
# state under infra/ and are mounted read-only or read-write at run time
# (docker/docker-compose.yaml:250-262). Copying them in would both bloat the
# image and ship user data inside it.
data/
logs/
*.log
service/weights/
weights/
pretrained_ckpts/
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.npy
*.ckpt

# --- SQL dumps other than the one the image NEEDS -------------------------
# service/infrastructure/database/schema.py resolves "<DB>.sql" from
# BACKEND_ROOT/database, i.e. /app/database/HireSnap.sql, so the committed dump in
# backend/database/ is deliberately NOT ignored (backend/docker/Dockerfile, layer
# 3). Any OTHER dump is a developer's local export and must not enter the image:
# it may hold production rows.
*.sql.bak
*.sql.gz
*.dump
mysqldump*.sql
!HireSnap.sql

# --- tooling noise the server does not import -----------------------------
# scripts/ is the interactive developer bootstrap and the one-off seed job; no
# runtime module imports it (service/ is the only importable package).
scripts/
*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/
notebooks/
tests/
docs/
**/*.md
!requirements.txt
.mailmap
.editorconfig
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
